# 5. GUI with ImGui

This example displays an implicit surface (a sum of blobs and of Perlin noise), meshed by marching cubes at
each change of its parameters. The interface is the ImGui window of the program, so that all the settings are
in a single window and there is no HTML to write. In a slide, this window has to be readable on the projector,
and to stay consistent with the buttons of the slide.

